{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait","id":1373005,"title":"The looooong wait","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-05T11:00:28-08:00","id":1373005,"title":"The looooong wait","content":"We know all that stuff about OP hiring freelancers, the state of the industry, etc etc.<br /> <br /> However, there was an explicit statement by OP about them being interested in accelerating the publication of Exalted material (around the time when the new devs came on board).<br /> <br /> However, I feel like the glacial pace hasn't gotten any faster really. We have WFHW, Arms, the Realm, and the Lunars manuscript sure, but... the ST guide, those essays I couldn't care less, the DB and the Lunar companion, Across the eight, and now also EE look very very VERY far on the horizon.<br /> <br /> (Oh, and by the way, I don't count the monthly enemies and characters as real additions. I don't use such material since Antagonist/PC balance in Exalted is almost non-existent.)<br /> <br /> My point is, I don't think the plan is working OPP guys. It's been a year since the Lunar KS and two since the DB KS, and Heirs to the Shogunate hasn't arrive yet. At this rate EE will be available around 2030. This makes me sad, I really want to stay excited for this game, but even if I get to read any of the books mentioned above, my friends have lost ALL hope and faith in this game.<br /> <br /> Bah... I know I'm not getting anything from this rant, but hey... this is almost everything I have to share about the whole Exalted topic, and this is the Exalted forum so...<br /> <br /> What do others think about all this? Have elepants and random monsters published monthly been enough to satiate your exalted hunger?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T11:53:21-08:00","id":1373022,"title":"","content":"According to the last Monday Meeting, Lunars is now in layout, so I\u2019d expect it to drop in something like six months. <br /> <br /> They\u2019re working on compiling Hundred Devils and Adversaries right now, but since they already have the art and stuff for many of those, I\u2019d expect that to go quickly.<br /> <br /> I admit, I kind of expected the DB companion to be out last summer, but the DB KS hit enough stretch goals that that\u2019s basically a normal sized softcover, and it apparently ran into some production issues.<br /> <br /> Given that the Devs are currently working on the DB companion, the Lunars companion, Across the Eight Directions, and Exigents, with Exigents being probably the hardest Exalted book to write ever, I\u2019m not really surprised that there\u2019s been a slowdown.<br /> <br /> Once they can put a couple of those books to bed, I think things will improve. On the upside, Hundred Devils, Adversaries, the ST Guide, and Essence are all being handled by other Devs, so they shouldn\u2019t slow things down too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T11:56:22-08:00","id":1373025,"title":"","content":"I have heard this complaint before, but have not personally experienced it... I think that they have put forth more than enough content, and continue to do so... But obviously, this has been at a pace that many find slower than what they would prefer. I prefer the high quality that we have been receiving, and that does not come with a 3+ Major Books a year publication schedule. Of course, I may be in the minority here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T12:02:46-08:00","id":1373027,"title":"","content":"The system's effectively dead to me until Crucible of Legend comes out and unless it covers the horrible failings of the corebook I need addressed, so I know exactly what you're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T12:12:14-08:00","id":1373029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373025#post1373025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have heard this complaint before, but have not personally experienced it... I think that they have put forth more than enough content, and continue to do so... But obviously, this has been at a pace that many find slower than what they would prefer. I prefer the high quality that we have been receiving, and that does not come with a 3+ Major Books a year publication schedule. Of course, I may be in the minority here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, that's understandable.<br /> <br /> As fo the higher quality, in my personal case, I stopped caring about Ex3 mechanics like two years ago. I'm not gonna read the tons of pages of lunar charms at this point, Ex3 is too heavy a system for my current needs. So what I'm looking for mainly are the new setting elements. I'm curious about new exalts and it's a bit annoying to read just scraps of something for years and years to come.<br /> <br /> Right now I'm writing my own custom Ex engine. I don't have plans to share it cause I don't think it will be what others like for their games. I wish I could have the ST guide to be able to comprehend the direction Abyssals, Infernals and others will have.<br /> <br /> Exalted Essence could be my wish come true, but 1) there's no guarantee for that, and 2) it's like five years away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T12:13:48-08:00","id":1373031,"title":"","content":"Well, the essays maybe, but Hundred Devil Night Parade and Adversaries of the Righteous are 100% actual content. You might not like them or use them, but they are content. They're also not all bad, there's just a lot of them that aren't powerful enough to challenge a lot of PC groups, which is arguably a player problem rather than a game problem, but it's really hard to argue that players shouldn't game the game aspect of the game.<br /> <br /> Some of the other stuff though is good. Mahicara can actually fight an entire circle of Solars on its own and be a pretty damn hard fight at that. There's Grelidaka, who's mechanics actually make it straight up invincible to any normal forms of damage, and in fact only serve to make it stronger. Face that against your Dawn and watch as he blows 30 motes and 3 willpower only to turn a small flock of deadly birds into millions of them.<br /> <br /> As for the other stuff, I'm not sure when it's coming out, but I'm pretty okay with the pace so far. I'm pretty sure that Heirs and the Exigent kickstarter are going to be coming out soon, and there's a lot of stuff that's actually in the pipe coming down, not counting essays or novellas: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Across the Eight Directions: Creation wide setting book</li> <li>Heirs to the Shogunate: Dragonblooded companion book</li> <li>Many-Faced Strangers: Lunar companion book</li> <li>Crucible of Legends: Storyteller handbook (about damned time...)</li> <li>Exigent Manuscript</li> <li>Full release of Hundred Devils Night Parade: A book containing lots of not-powerful-enough enemies...but also a behemoth and a third circle demon</li> <li>Exalted Essence Edition: Rules-lite demi edition with rules for every type of Exalt</li> <li>Adversaries of the Righteous: A book containing even more antagonists, although ones that may present themselves as possible allies/rivals</li> </ol><br /> That's really not too bad. It doesn't quite match up to DnD's book release schedule, but it's not far behind, and DnD is a way easier system to design for with a lot more resources.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Exalted Essence, it's being worked on by a totally different set of writers, many of whom have been playing Exalted since 1st edition and writing for Exalted since at least 2nd edition, so EE doesn't impact the mainline content very much. I don't think we should expect it out this year, but I'd be surprised if it wasn't out sometime in 2021.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T12:17:01-08:00","id":1373033,"title":"","content":"What's important is not the destination, but the friends we made along the way. *eyes sparkle*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T12:22:33-08:00","id":1373035,"title":"","content":"It's always good to read you Dr! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373031#post1373031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Exalted Essence, it's being worked on by a totally different set of writers, many of whom have been playing Exalted since 1st edition and writing for Exalted since at least 2nd edition, so EE doesn't impact the mainline content very much. I don't think we should expect it out this year, but I'd be surprised if it wasn't out sometime in 2021.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, I know that we now have several groups of developers, but there's somewhere in the process that makes that lunars is in &quot;art is ready&quot; state for months, and which I believe is beyond any and all devs' to solve. This worries me a lot. Because new cool and awesome books are being added to the line, and almost none are getting released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T12:45:14-08:00","id":1373043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373031#post1373031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the essays maybe, but Hundred Devil Night Parade and Adversaries of the Righteous are 100% actual content. You might not like them or use them, but they are content. They're also not all bad, there's just a lot of them that aren't powerful enough to challenge a lot of PC groups, which is arguably a player problem rather than a game problem, but it's really hard to argue that players shouldn't game the game aspect of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until a book comes out saying what the chargen expectations the system is based in are, it's 100% a game problem that players are getting scapegoated for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T13:32:38-08:00","id":1373058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373035#post1373035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right, I know that we now have several groups of developers, but there's somewhere in the process that makes that lunars is in &quot;art is ready&quot; state for months, and which I believe is beyond any and all devs' to solve. This worries me a lot. Because new cool and awesome books are being added to the line, and almost none are getting released.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Exalted Essence were being billed as Exalted 4th edition then I'd say next year would be too optimistic. Rules-lite stuff goes quickly though. Not instantly quickly, they still have to debate about how light to make the system exactly, but they don't have to try and balance 800 charms or anything. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373043#post1373043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Until a book comes out saying what the chargen expectations the system is based in are, it's 100% a game problem that players are getting scapegoated for.</div> </div> </div> </div>It...kind of does, but it's clearly not enough. The corebook says that any attribute or ability rated over 2 dots requires and in-character explanation to justify them, and the quickstart characters all have really wide ranging combat abilities. On the other hand clearly that's not enough for many, maybe even most, tables and there's still a ton of people that tack on &quot;Combat god&quot; onto whatever else their concept involves.<br /> <br /> On the other-other hand if Crucible of Legends comes out and in big bold letters says &quot;Unless you're the circle's Dawn, don't take more than 2 dots in a combat ability!&quot; will that actually make a difference or will people just keep doing it anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T13:55:10-08:00","id":1373067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373058#post1373058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It...kind of does, but it's clearly not enough. The corebook says that any attribute or ability rated over 2 dots requires and in-character explanation to justify them, and the quickstart characters all have really wide ranging combat abilities. On the other hand clearly that's not enough for many, maybe even most, tables and there's still a ton of people that tack on &quot;Combat god&quot; onto whatever else their concept involves.<br /> <br /> On the other-other hand if Crucible of Legends comes out and in big bold letters says &quot;Unless you're the circle's Dawn, don't take more than 2 dots in a combat ability!&quot; will that actually make a difference or will people just keep doing it anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, more scapegoating. <br /> The <b>problem</b> is that the system clearly has some expectation of what numbers will be thrown around. Not just for combat, not just maxima. Certain ranges in which it behaves well, for <b>all pools</b>. But it doesn't communicate them. <br /> How many dice is &quot;right&quot; for a starting Dawn to be strong but not overwhelmingly strong? To win, but have fun back-and-forth in doing so? Bloody fuck if I know, book doesn't say a word. <br /> And what about other characters? How many dice should the &quot;present in every fight but not fight-centric&quot; folk have to not feel like they're hopelessly flailing at superior foes but not steal the Dawn's thunder or turn the Circle into a five-man blending team? Whoops, zero advice in the book! <br /> What about a socialite, how many dice is &quot;right&quot; to sway often and be swayed occasionally, to have a fun ebb and flow in the ballrooms and conference halls? Again, bloody fucking book doesn't say. <br /> What about an admiral? How many dice should my &quot;Captained a boat once, was OK at it&quot; have to give the party a chance in a naval battle but make alternatives a better choice? Ha, just kidding I know the book would never have useful information like that in it. <br /> <br /> You're getting tunnel-vision over big combat numbers. I can't blame you, they're very obvious when they're a problem. But they also lead to the scapegoating of players who make good decisions. The problem is much, much more than the ease of big combat numbers. The problem is a complete lack of guidance regarding numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T14:47:39-08:00","id":1373076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373067#post1373067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're getting tunnel-vision over big combat numbers. I can't blame you, they're very obvious when they're a problem. But they also lead to the scapegoating of players who make good decisions. The problem is much, much more than the ease of big combat numbers. The problem is a complete lack of guidance regarding numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Scapegoating players?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373031#post1373031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's really hard to argue that players shouldn't game the game aspect of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1305398-exalted-arena?p=1370656#post1370656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s hard to tell them no though. I mean, they can make a powerful character, or choose to make a weak one deliberately, it\u2019s really hard to resist doing the former.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As for &quot;How many dots should my character who does X have.&quot; I don't think that's particularly without guidance. If you've captained a ship one time maybe one dot? Professional enlisted soldiers have 2 dots of melee, if you want to be a particularly standout socialite take 3 dots, if you want to be Loki take 5 dots. Which is kind of context dependent anyway, your character with 3 socialize might have an easy time messing around with a court of mortals out in the Threshold, but is going to encounter some pretty serious trouble when faced with a Great House Matriarch. Two dots of Sail makes you a match for any regular pirate, but against the Admiral of the Water Fleet you'll probably fall short.<br /> <br /> There's also another chart for dicepools on page 495-496. It's just way too easy, I think, to randomly pick up something and become nearly unstoppable with it. Not just combat, if you want you grab 5 Integrity and bam, you're an immutable rock of Resolve, especially with the free Solar excellency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T14:47:57-08:00","id":1373077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait#post1373005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know all that stuff about OP hiring freelancers, the state of the industry, etc etc.<br /> <br /> However, there was an explicit statement by OP about them being interested in accelerating the publication of Exalted material (around the time when the new devs came on board).<br /> <br /> However, I feel like the glacial pace hasn't gotten any faster really. We have WFHW, Arms, the Realm, and the Lunars manuscript sure, but... the ST guide, those essays I couldn't care less, the DB and the Lunar companion, Across the eight, and now also EE look very very VERY far on the horizon.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly is the thing here though to do? THey are throwing hte man power they can at it. It simply is that they can only do so much with entirely freelance temas. Note that a lot of this isn't even very mechanical. At8D is mostly fluff, but it doesn't as you noitce, go any faster. There's only so much wordcount that can be written and editted in so much time. So yeah, it's slow, but there's nothing OPP to a point to make it faster unless you have a solution to be honest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait#post1373005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Oh, and by the way, I don't count the monthly enemies and characters as real additions. I don't use such material since Antagonist/PC balance in Exalted is almost non-existent.)<br /> <br /> My point is, I don't think the plan is working OPP guys. It's been a year since the Lunar KS and two since the DB KS, and Heirs to the Shogunate hasn't arrive yet. At this rate EE will be available around 2030. This makes me sad, I really want to stay excited for this game, but even if I get to read any of the books mentioned above, my friends have lost ALL hope and faith in this game.<br /> <br /> Bah... I know I'm not getting anything from this rant, but hey... this is almost everything I have to share about the whole Exalted topic, and this is the Exalted forum so...<br /> <br /> What do others think about all this? Have elepants and random monsters published monthly been enough to satiate your exalted hunger?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I use the hell out of a few and the <b>Adversaries</b> stuff especially is full of good plot hooks. And the QCs in HDNP is really good not just as-are but for expanding the setting and giving pools of powers to yoink for constructing my own creatures. I liked them a lot and look forward to the compiled volumes myself.<br /> <br /> But again, &quot;Plan isn't working' assumes there's some option somewhere bsides &quot;Don't do a second draft&quot; as far as I gather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T15:24:03-08:00","id":1373084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373076#post1373076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for &quot;How many dots should my character who does X have.&quot; I don't think that's particularly without guidance. If you've captained a ship one time maybe one dot? Professional enlisted soldiers have 2 dots of melee, if you want to be a particularly standout socialite take 3 dots, if you want to be Loki take 5 dots. Which is kind of context dependent anyway, your character with 3 socialize might have an easy time messing around with a court of mortals out in the Threshold, but is going to encounter some pretty serious trouble when faced with a Great House Matriarch. Two dots of Sail makes you a match for any regular pirate, but against the Admiral of the Water Fleet you'll probably fall short.<br /> <br /> There's also another chart for dicepools on page 495-496. It's just way too easy, I think, to randomly pick up something and become nearly unstoppable with it. Not just combat, if you want you grab 5 Integrity and bam, you're an immutable rock of Resolve, especially with the free Solar excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanical guidance, not fluff. Guidance on pools, X+Y. Not X, not Y, X+Y. For PCs. The guidelines you point to are fucking useless for PCs. <b>Three to six dice</b> &quot;is a fair challenge for players\u2019 characters who are moderately to significantly invested in that area&quot;? <i><b>Bullshit</b></i>. PCs get into that dice range with <b>Attributes</b>. Not even Excellencies or Abilities, just Attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T17:28:19-08:00","id":1373104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373084#post1373084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mechanical guidance, not fluff. Guidance on pools, X+Y. Not X, not Y, X+Y. For PCs. The guidelines you point to are fucking useless for PCs. <b>Three to six dice</b> &amp;quot;is a fair challenge for players\u2019 characters who are moderately to significantly invested in that area&amp;quot;? <i><b>Bullshit</b></i>. PCs get into that dice range with <b>Attributes</b>. Not even Excellencies or Abilities, just Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having six dice in something IS moderately to significantly invested in an area. If you\u2019ve got 5 manipulation you are one of the most manipulative people in the entire direction. When that person breezes past enemy\u2019s Read Intention rolls with her essence boosted Guile of 9 that part is working fine. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s just too easy to deeply invest in lots of important stuff. If you want you can get 5s in Awareness, Integrity and Melee and be unable to be convinced of anything, unable to be snuck up on, and unable to lose a fight to all but dedicated enemy exalted or massively overwhelming odds. That doesn\u2019t take even half of your chargen resources and you can go crazy with the rest, probably throw resistance in there too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T18:07:21-08:00","id":1373113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373029#post1373029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not gonna read the tons of pages of lunar charms at this point</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T18:11:21-08:00","id":1373114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373077#post1373077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Plan isn't working' assumes there's some option somewhere bsides &quot;Don't do a second draft&quot; as far as I gather.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is real curiosity: what was it that they were doing or not doing in Ex2 to release the books so fast? I know that no quality control was one of the things, but it seemed like everything else, art, editing, etc went a lot faster. Again, Lunars, a rules heavy hardcover, was already written like eight months ago?, and it's still traped in layout hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T18:29:13-08:00","id":1373120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373113#post1373113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're missing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there charms about duplicating or re-rolling a certain number depending on how many extra successes you got after succesfully winning a read intentions action during the previous two rounds of combat?<br /> <br /> If so, not interested, not at all.<br /> <br /> If not. Well... I guess you're right, but I just can't dig a set of powers based on a system that is meant for computers to run against each other.<br /> <br /> Robert Vance is a genius, I'm sure of it, but I wish the entire Ex3 system was not so convoluted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T19:07:24-08:00","id":1373123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373114#post1373114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is real curiosity: what was it that they were doing or not doing in Ex2 to release the books so fast? I know that no quality control was one of the things, but it seemed like everything else, art, editing, etc went a lot faster. Again, Lunars, a rules heavy hardcover, was already written like eight months ago?, and it's still traped in layout hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>So to my understanding with speaking with previous writers, there was little to no actual changes of second drafts to developed book. Additionally is just resources. Onyx Path is a smaller company than mid-to-late-00s White Wolf. Note for instance that Exalted use to have its own dedicated art director and layout (Brian Glass). Right now, OPP doesn't have the resources for that.<br /> <br /> Like, straight-up, think about how the 2e book <b>Scroll of Heroes</b> in the god-blooded chapter 1) Assumed god-bloods channeled Essence (they didn't before), 2) Had an idea of &quot;places of sin&quot; for demon-blooded (which never existed before) and 3) Had Merits for Moon-Touched based on Charms Lunars had in 1e they didn't in 2e. I kind of severely doubt that would ship in 3e as that is.<br /> <br /> It also had, again, full-time devs and authors. That's another factor that makes things harder to do. The resources aren't there, and this generates bottle necks which unfortunately hangs things up. I'm not a games developer, but I am pretty sure that the folks in charge would like stuff out faster too. The realities of the process means it's not, and the reasons for that are not clear beyond more bottlenecks than before, and a different feel on quality control an dhow to manage it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T19:13:14-08:00","id":1373124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373120#post1373120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there charms about duplicating or re-rolling a certain number depending on how many extra successes you got after succesfully winning a read intentions action during the previous two rounds of combat?<br /> <br /> If so, not interested, not at all.<br /> <br /> If not. Well... I guess you're right, but I just can't dig a set of powers based on a system that is meant for computers to run against each other.<br /> <br /> Robert Vance is a genius, I'm sure of it, but I wish the entire Ex3 system was not so convoluted.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth I just went through the first 50 charms in the Lunar book and 4 of them were dice tricks, I'm not sure if you consider that a lot or not. I can't really talk though because I haven't gone through the whole charmset either. I'm not playing a lunars game any time soon and don't really need to know them that intricately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T22:25:41-08:00","id":1373155,"title":"","content":"I'm personally wondering what's so different that we haven't gotten a Lunars backer PDF yet. We had WFHW I think 9-ish months after, but with Lunars we're at over 12 with barely a peep.<br /> <br /> Exalted is my favorite game of all time, and I was ecstatic when dev changed hands and we had that surge of content, but even I'm having an increasingly hard time keeping my spirits up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T01:45:15-08:00","id":1373164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373120#post1373120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there charms about duplicating or re-rolling a certain number depending on how many extra successes you got after succesfully winning a read intentions action during the previous two rounds of combat?<br /> <br /> If so, not interested, not at all.<br /> <br /> If not. Well... I guess you're right, but I just can't dig a set of powers based on a system that is meant for computers to run against each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, the first few words of this inquiry had me thinking it would have been after the Lunar Charms that allow them to duplicate themselves.<br /> <br /> They're at the back of Dexterity.<br /> <br /> What actually is the upper limit for acceptable mathematics in an RPG?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Robert Vance is a genius, I'm sure of it, but I wish the entire Ex3 system was not so convoluted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Credit for those Charms is due to other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T05:36:45-08:00","id":1373180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373155#post1373155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm personally wondering what's so different that we haven't gotten a Lunars backer PDF yet. We had WFHW I think 9-ish months after, but with Lunars we're at over 12 with barely a peep.</div> </div> </div> </div>We also had the Lunars kickstarter last March, and the Dragonblood kickstarter the March before, so I was hoping to see Exigents about now, but there haven't even been any previews of it.<br /> <br /> Still, it's very difficult to count these things. The rate has been better than the previous Devs, so...<br /> <br /> Tbh, whether you complain or are happy with the rate, isn't going to make much difference. I've got Lunars and Dragonblood, which were the books I really needed, so while the wait was really annoying before, I don't care too much now. I now feel I can run the game I want, so any more books that get released are nice, but not essential.<br /> I would quite like the final release of Hundred Devils Night Parade though, if it has a bunch more high-level enemies. That would be useful. I think Exalted: Essence would be useful for our high-level games too.<br /> I may well buy Exigents, Across the Eight Directions, etc, but they're not really essential for me, like Lunars and Dragonblood were.<br /> <br /> I can well see that if, say, the thing you love most about Exalted is Abyssals or Sidereals, it must be pretty irritating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-06-2020, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T07:13:42-08:00","id":1373196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373180#post1373180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, it's very difficult to count these things. The rate has been better than the previous Devs, so...<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Very very barely...actually, not at all depending on what you count. Unless we assume that the old Dev team was going to take multiple years to complete every book, the rate has been about 1 book a year:<br /> Exalted Core (we'll not count the Miracles Book, for fairness) 2016<br /> Arms of the Chosen (Nov. 2017--Old Devs credited but this is transistion, as by all reports I've heard, the Old Devs took a number of notes with them)<br /> Dragonblooded (Out to Backers in late 2018, Public Apr 2019.)<br /> The Realm (July 2019)<br /> <br /> So, we have an average of 1 book per year, for 4 years(new Devs did not have a book out for the public 2018). I am not counting Lunars, because the book is not finished nor for sale, nor do we have when it finished development.My own observation, from Monday Meeting Notes, is that things tend to stockpile near Art and Layout, not second draft.<br /> Now, Hundred Devils and Adversaries fill that gap well--but lets be frank, those are not products that take up the same resources. Perhaps they are an innovation of Vance and Erics--thats possible, I don't know. But when it comes to full, core setting material, the rate has been about the same.<br /> Now I'm fine with this. I have enough material to run my games. I'd rather have <i>more</i>. I'd rather have my infernals and more demons and my sidereals etc. But I will be greatly impressed if the rate increases to a consistent 2 books a year. The issue with timeline does not seem to have been with the developers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T07:22:15-08:00","id":1373197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373180#post1373180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We also had the Lunars kickstarter last March, and the Dragonblood kickstarter the March before, so I was hoping to see Exigents about now, but there haven't even been any previews of it.<br /> <br /> Still, it's very difficult to count these things. The rate has been better than the previous Devs, so...<br /> <br /> Tbh, whether you complain or are happy with the rate, isn't going to make much difference. I've got Lunars and Dragonblood, which were the books I really needed, so while the wait was really annoying before, I don't care too much now. I now feel I can run the game I want, so any more books that get released are nice, but not essential.<br /> I would quite like the final release of Hundred Devils Night Parade though, if it has a bunch more high-level enemies. That would be useful. I think Exalted: Essence would be useful for our high-level games too.<br /> I may well buy Exigents, Across the Eight Directions, etc, but they're not really essential for me, like Lunars and Dragonblood were.<br /> <br /> I can well see that if, say, the thing you love most about Exalted is Abyssals or Sidereals, it must be pretty irritating.</div> </div> </div> </div>My favorites are Abyssals and Alchemicals, though I understand why those come later. That's not the source of what bugs me. <br /> <br /> The PDF we have of Lunars is miserable to use and even though it's taking a good bit longer we have no real communication as to what's going on.<br /> Exigents or the STs guide are essential tools for effectively emulating pretty much everything else, including the brand new to this edition entire Exalt types and we have little to know communication about what's going on there.<br /> We're still waiting on Heirs, as well stated by prior posters.<br /> This one isn't a dev thing, but just buying all the PDFs for HDNP and Adversaries well exceed the cost of a hardbound book but we haven't heard a peep on what, if anything, already having bought most/all PDFs will do to costs of the print copy.<br /> And, frankly, one of the things that gets to me more than almost anything else is that we have this newly expanded Creation with tons of new places and environments, but yet for so many we have maybe a sentence or two about them, new Exalt types with, at best, a couple QCs. We don't even have that for Germans. 3rd Edition has always been supposed to be this big breath of fresh air with a ton of new content to reinvigorate the setting, but at this point we barely have the basics.<br /> <br /> I'm not wanting 1E or 2E's release schedule, but I'd really like some communication and clarity. Exalted is almost never discussed on the PathCast, the &quot;Exalted deep dive&quot; twitch interview barely talked about Exalted, it's non-existent on any of the OPP streaming. I'm not demanding everything, I'm just asking for SOMETHING","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 03-06-2020, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T07:47:05-08:00","id":1373202,"title":"","content":"There is actually some communication, but it happens mostly on the Discord. Here are the ones I've seen :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton (2/8/2020)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigents won't have a Kickstarter for a few months yet. Various project members have been hit by personal issues that have delayed progress on the line. We're in the process of getting back on track, but March is off the table.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton (Yesterday)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going forward, we've been [bringing] on more developers to whom we can assign things like Kickstarter companion books; that's what we're doing with Many-Faced Strangers, which Vance and I have hardly looked at while someone else takes point on development.<br /> As to Heirs, well, mistakes were made, from which we are hopefully taking the right lessons.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 03-06-2020, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T07:59:13-08:00","id":1373206,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: Jade Cricket (The Freedom Stone) is one of the writers for Crucible of Legends (ST Guide) and Exalted: Essence. This is mostly a side-comment, but is relevant insofar as an example of them hiring more folks to help with writing content (which I admit doesn't help the development/layout bottleneck).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T08:07:53-08:00","id":1373208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373202#post1373202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is actually some communication, but it happens mostly on the Discord. Here are the ones I've seen :<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate the insight.<br /> <br /> That said, Discord moves so fast and isn't always accessible to everyone. Answer questions in the moment, sure, but it's a REALLY shifty way to keep a fan base at large. Unless you're looking at the chat at the exact moment, there's mountains of chaff to sift through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T08:33:48-08:00","id":1373211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373208#post1373208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the insight.<br /> <br /> That said, Discord moves so fast and isn't always accessible to everyone. Answer questions in the moment, sure, but it's a REALLY shifty way to keep a fan base at large. Unless you're looking at the chat at the exact moment, there's mountains of chaff to sift through.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Exalted Discord, hit Ctrl+F.<br /> \u200bType into the search bar: &quot;from: Eric Minton#9481&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's a list of all Eric's posts in the Exalted Discord, with the most recent appearing first.<br /> <br /> &quot;from: Vance#7504&quot; would be everything Robert Vance has said.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you just want to <i>just</i> see Vance's puppy-related posts, you'd type &quot;from: Vance#7504 puppy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Discord has a reasonably sophisticated chaff-sifting machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T09:53:16-08:00","id":1373218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373211#post1373211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Exalted Discord, hit Ctrl+F.<br /> \u200bType into the search bar: &quot;from: Eric Minton#9481&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat's a list of all Eric's posts in the Exalted Discord, with the most recent appearing first.<br /> <br /> &quot;from: Vance#7504&quot; would be everything Robert Vance has said.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you just want to <i>just</i> see Vance's puppy-related posts, you'd type &quot;from: Vance#7504 puppy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Discord has a reasonably sophisticated chaff-sifting machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am quite familiar with Discord. Not knowing how to search isn't the problem, I'm fully familiar with the search function. But unlike, say, the MMN which are static, easy to locate, and can be pulled up in a browser for reading at your leisure, even sifting down to only Minton or Vance's posts still doesn't narrow it down further to only development related content. There's <i>only</i> 4235 posts from Minton in the General channel alone, and in the first thirty so (at time of typing]) only one or two are development related.<br /> <br /> And sometimes Discord is inaccessible, or immensely inconvenient. Search works great on PC, less so on mobile browser or app.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","user":"SamuraiMujuru","date":". 03-06-2020, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T17:44:49-08:00","id":1373288,"title":"","content":"I would buy and read 10 times the published Exalted 3rd edition hard-back and soft-back content. In its lack, I re-read 1st and 2nd edition, and do my best at fan-conversions. <br /> <br /> Hundred Devils Night Parade is not the content I'm looking for, though I will still buy and read it it in compiled format.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T18:02:42-08:00","id":1373290,"title":"","content":"I want to expand on why I'm not looking for HDNP content. If I'm going to have to re-work all the numbers and abilities and Intimacies of an antagonist and their entourage to challenge my Celestial Circle, I already own Creatures of the Wyld, Games of Divinity, Roll of Glorious Divinity I and II, literally 11 Celestial/Terrestrial directions books with a monster chapter each, etc. My players are all pretty new to Exalted, and I'm the one whose enthusiasm (and willingness to ST) makes the table happen, so just because Ligier was first published something like 18 years ago, does not dampen his glory in the least when he is introduced to my table (I have not yet done so). Like, who has run out of cool published antagonists for Exalted? I want that group's schedule.<br /> <br /> What I want are a full set of workable, playable, PC-capable Exalts types for 3rd Edition, which are much harder to homebrew (I've tried!). 3rd Ed. Solars are awesome. So are Lunars. So are Dragon-Blooded. But my players want to be Sidereals and Alchemicals and Infernals and Abyssals. They come to the table with a hunger for themes that Solars can't provide. But Exalted can provide for that player's aesthetic! And the corebook is very explicit that these flavors of Exalted exist! <br /> <br /> Basically, I'm ready to buy a half-dozen more books when they come out. Or are kicked or whatever. Just not more antagonists. I'm drowning in them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T00:55:09-08:00","id":1373496,"title":"","content":"The one delay that bites for me is Heirs. <br /> <br /> I'm not fussed about the rest of the line: Onyx Path's resources are far from limitless, but it's starting to feel like the devs just really wanted to do anything but that book. We've had a bunch of new projects enter the system since then, it seems likely we'll have two Kickstarters run, creating more companion books, and the first one has been sitting at development for how long? Everything else I'm willing to accept but that just feels mismanaged. And it kinda kills any motivation to back further Kickstarters at a high tier - why should I pay for a unique charm or artifact if the devs are going to put that project on the backburner like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T01:56:33-08:00","id":1373502,"title":"","content":"I think the devs did admit that there was some sort of production problem with Heirs. Problems with the writers or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T21:39:22-07:00","id":1373840,"title":"","content":"Another MMN comes and goes without any listed Exalted progress. \ud83d\ude11","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T06:06:42-07:00","id":1373902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373840#post1373840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another MMN comes and goes without any listed Exalted progress. \ud83d\ude11</div> </div> </div> </div>I can say that <b>Essence</b> is making absolutely huge strides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T07:02:29-07:00","id":1373913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373902#post1373902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can say that <b>Essence</b> is making absolutely huge strides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is grand, but that's something I expect to be a year out at least, and the only Exalted thing that got a bolded change of status in ages was the DB novella. As much as I'm looking forward to Essence, I'd much prefer anything approaching clarity on when we might expect to see a Lunars backer PDF, or the early pdfs for AotR or HDNP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T07:41:49-07:00","id":1373920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373913#post1373913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is grand, but that's something I expect to be a year out at least, and the only Exalted thing that got a bolded change of status in ages was the DB novella. As much as I'm looking forward to Essence, I'd much prefer anything approaching clarity on when we might expect to see a Lunars backer PDF, or the early pdfs for AotR or HDNP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t expect the Lunar backer pdf to come out before Heirs to the Shogunate. Considering that book has to go through manuscript approval, editing, post editing development and layout, that\u2019s at least two months away. Adversaries and HDNP are a bit trickier to guess because of the way they were made, but I would say pretty confidently that we won\u2019t get them before June. I\u2019d be very surprised if they weren\u2019t out by August though. <br /> <br /> My personal guess for what we\u2019ll get by this year\u2019s end is Exigents manuscript, Heirs to the Shogunate, Lunar full release, Adversaries of the Righteous, Across Eight Directions and Crucible of Legends. I kind of doubt many faced strangers will be but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Also various novellas and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T07:49:00-07:00","id":1373923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373496#post1373496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one delay that bites for me is Heirs.<br /> <br /> I'm not fussed about the rest of the line: Onyx Path's resources are far from limitless, but it's starting to feel like the devs just really wanted to do anything but that book. We've had a bunch of new projects enter the system since then, it seems likely we'll have two Kickstarters run, creating more companion books, and the first one has been sitting at development for how long? Everything else I'm willing to accept but that just feels mismanaged. And it kinda kills any motivation to back further Kickstarters at a high tier - why should I pay for a unique charm or artifact if the devs are going to put that project on the backburner like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heirs is not &quot;sitting&quot; in development; it's not on the back burner. Other than getting pulled off of it for a couple of weeks for <i>Lunars </i>post-editing development, Vance and I have had <i>Heirs </i>as our primary focus for months. The manuscript has required significantly more extensive development work than other manuscripts we've worked on before or (so far) since. I am very much looking forward to finishing it off so that I can start focusing on other projects again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T08:13:04-07:00","id":1373928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373923#post1373923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heirs is not &amp;quot;sitting&amp;quot; in development; it's not on the back burner. Other than getting pulled off of it for a couple of weeks for <i>Lunars </i>post-editing development, Vance and I have had <i>Heirs </i>as our primary focus for months. The manuscript has required significantly more extensive development work than other manuscripts we've worked on before or (so far) since. I am very much looking forward to finishing it off so that I can start focusing on other projects again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heirs is pretty big too right? Something like 30 new charms, 10 QCs, half a dozen other characters, Lookshy expansion x3, Forest Witch expansion x3, outcasts expansion x3, Realm expansion x4, Cadet House expansion x2, Prasad expansion x2, and chapter fictions.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not really like the Miracles of the Solar Exalted companion book was for the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T08:16:53-07:00","id":1373931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373928#post1373928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heirs is pretty big too right? Something like 30 new charms, 10 QCs, half a dozen other characters, Lookshy expansion x3, Forest Witch expansion x3, outcasts expansion x3, Realm expansion x4, Cadet House expansion x2, Prasad expansion x2, and chapter fictions.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not really like the Miracles of the Solar Exalted companion book was for the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's slated to be about 40% larger than <i>Arms of the Chosen</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T08:25:19-07:00","id":1373933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373931#post1373931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's slated to be about 40% larger than <i>Arms of the Chosen</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Niiice. Looking forward to it for my DB game this summer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T08:28:06-07:00","id":1373935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373920#post1373920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn\u2019t expect the Lunar backer pdf to come out before Heirs to the Shogunate. Considering that book has to go through manuscript approval, editing, post editing development and layout, that\u2019s at least two months away. Adversaries and HDNP are a bit trickier to guess because of the way they were made, but I would say pretty confidently that we won\u2019t get them before June. I\u2019d be very surprised if they weren\u2019t out by August though. <br /> <br /> My personal guess for what we\u2019ll get by this year\u2019s end is Exigents manuscript, Heirs to the Shogunate, Lunar full release, Adversaries of the Righteous, Across Eight Directions and Crucible of Legends. I kind of doubt many faced strangers will be but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Also various novellas and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>My frame of reference is WFHW. The Kickstarter completed in April of 18 and we had the backer PDF that following December. <br /> <br /> It's certainly possible Lunars has been a much more complicated book than DB, but if that's the case I haven't seen that communicated anywhere. All I know right now is we're about a year out from the Lunars KS and presumably layout is going to be at bare minimum another month.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T09:42:33-07:00","id":1373942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373935#post1373935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My frame of reference is WFHW. The Kickstarter completed in April of 18 and we had the backer PDF that following December. <br /> <br /> It's certainly possible Lunars has been a much more complicated book than DB, but if that's the case I haven't seen that communicated anywhere. All I know right now is we're about a year out from the Lunars KS and presumably layout is going to be at bare minimum another month.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s probably not much more complex than WFHW, more likely it\u2019s just scheduling based. The timelines with the layout person didn\u2019t line up as well, and then once it rolled past the holiday season you lose more time as production slows. According to Mike Chany Lunar layout is going to take up his whole March, which probably means backer PDF in April, unless it gets bogged down in approval somehow.<br /> <br /> If Minton is right that Heirs is 40% bigger than Arms that means it\u2019s well over half the size of WFHW, and if Many Faced Strangers continues along those lines it\u2019s a ton of content to write and edit, which is why I can\u2019t see it coming this year with Eight Directions and Crucible still to go. HDNP and AotR are both kind of weird in that they\u2019ve been getting art and layout and stuff monthly, but compiling them into one book and adding the characters that weren\u2019t in the monthly supplements is still going to take a lot of time, and Exigents is going to be in layout after the Kickstarter as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T09:53:24-07:00","id":1373943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373902#post1373902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can say that <b>Essence</b> is making absolutely huge strides.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good to hear. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T11:01:54-07:00","id":1373949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373942#post1373942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s probably not much more complex than WFHW, more likely it\u2019s just scheduling based. The timelines with the layout person didn\u2019t line up as well, and then once it rolled past the holiday season you lose more time as production slows. According to Mike Chany Lunar layout is going to take up his whole March, which probably means backer PDF in April, unless it gets bogged down in approval somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is all reasonable speculation, but my point continues to be that that's all it is. Speculation. There hasn't been any readily available updates stating scheduling pushed it to the holidays or the holidays pushing it back further. Not in MMN, nor in the backer updates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T12:24:51-07:00","id":1373967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373949#post1373949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is all reasonable speculation, but my point continues to be that that's all it is. Speculation. There hasn't been any readily available updates stating scheduling pushed it to the holidays or the holidays pushing it back further. Not in MMN, nor in the backer updates.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be nice to get some projections, yeah. We\u2019re not anywhere near ex3 corebook levels of stupidly frustrating though, where everyone kept talking up how soon it would be released three years before backers got even the manuscript so I try to keep perspective. We\u2019ve had the full text of the entire Lunar book since the day the Kickstarter ended its finding period, which is a massive improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-10T13:14:15-07:00","id":1373979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1373005-the-looooong-wait?p=1373967#post1373967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might be nice to get some projections, yeah. We\u2019re not anywhere near ex3 corebook levels of stupidly frustrating though, where everyone kept talking up how soon it would be released three years before backers got even the manuscript so I try to keep perspective. We\u2019ve had the full text of the entire Lunar book since the day the Kickstarter ended its finding period, which is a massive improvement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's not nearly as bad as EX3. But it's been a fair bit worse than WFHW, the only other frame of reference we have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T03:58:45-07:00","id":1374095,"title":"","content":"I'm just surprised that there are still people who seem to think that the speed of releases is going to somehow improve in a meaningful way. Onyx Path is a small operation, trying to handle many game lines, and as a result, slow to get books out the door. That isn't likely to change any time soon.<br /> <br /> This isn't necessarily a criticism - for a relatively small publisher trying to handle... what, at least nine distinct game lines? (and that's a low end estimate that lumps all the various vampire/werewolf/mage stuff under either Chronicles or World)... Well, when you look at it that way, one significant book a year per line is about all that can be expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}